## WHSLocDirStrategy Integration

### Strategy Pattern

D365FO uses the Strategy pattern for location directives:

```xpp
abstract class WHSLocDirStrategy
{
    public Query getQuery(WHSLocDirAction _action) {}
    public void setQuery(WHSLocDirAction _action, Query _query) {}
}

class WHSLocDirStrategyEmpty extends WHSLocDirStrategy {}
class WHSLocDirStrategyConsolidate extends WHSLocDirStrategy {}
class WHSLocDirStrategyLocation extends WHSLocDirStrategy {}
// etc.
```

### Strategy Construction

```xpp
WHSLocDirStrategy strategy = WHSLocDirStrategy::construct(_action.LocDirStrategyId);
```

### Query Retrieval via Strategy

Our helper class uses this pattern:

```xpp
public static Query getActionQuery(WHSLocDirAction _action)
{
    Query query;
    WHSLocDirStrategy strategy;
    
    strategy = WHSLocDirStrategy::construct(_action.LocDirStrategyId);
    
    if (strategy)
    {
        query = strategy.getQuery(_action);
    }
    
    return query;
}
```

**Note:** In practice, we found that reading `_action.QueryCriteria` directly is more reliable, as it always contains the current query state.

